        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          Fig. 1. - Schematic drawings of frontal sections of the medulla, showing the localization of Fos-positive cells in the vestibular nuclei of both sides in four representative rats of the FLT group sacrificed at FD2, FD14, R+1 and R+13, respectively.<br/>The number at the extreme right corner of each scheme corresponds to the stereotaxic plane of bregma (B) as reported in the atlas of appaxinos and Watson. At FD2 (R3) a discrete number of labeled cells occurred in the MVe and SpVe of both sides at caudal level, while scattered cells where found within the group F (FVe), the Pr and the IN as well as the ECu/X structures. At FD14 (R5) the number of labeled cells was particularly reduced with respect to that obtained at FD2 in all the structures indicated above. At R+1 (R17) there was a prominent and bilateral increase in number of labeled cells in the caudal part of MVe and SpVe (including the group F) and to some extent also in the nuclei ECu/X, but not in the Pr. However, a large number of labeled cells occurred in EF. At R+13 (R19) the number of labeled cells was greatly attenuated in all the structures indicated above, so as to reach the level obtained in rats of the simulated control group (AGC) sacrificed at the same time interval after return of the animal to 1 G. No labeled cells were found in the caudal half of the LVe at any time interval of the flight, as seen at more rostral levels (not shown).<br/>
        </div>

